<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Athos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Novy Afon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Athos (Novy Afon) is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast of Abkhazia, north-west of Sukhumi. Above it stand the ruins of the medieval fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anacopia">Anacopia</a>. The town takes its name from the New Athos Monastery, founded in 1875 by Russian monks from the Saint Panteleimon Monastery on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a>. It is also known for a large karst cave system, opened to visitors in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-athos.jpg" alt="New Athos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alaexis · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Athos_Monastery.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
